     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone!<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m new to ggplot2, and i&#39;m currently using plot_models from the package sjPlot to create a forest plot for multiple regression models. </div><div>I was following the first example here: <a href=\"http://www.strengejacke.de/sjPlot/reference/plot_models.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.strengejacke.de/sjPlot/reference/plot_models.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366336755000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03a9fwtgcaWjO9OJgVCVwj\">http://www.strengejacke.de/sjPlot/reference/plot_models.html</a></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(136,136,136);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:#800\"># fit three models</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">fit1</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(38,77,102);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(248